body:
### Bug Description
The maintenance tasks [spawned](https://github.com/launchbadge/sqlx/blob/c17c59fc4c13d5031f05b316ef8a8fb44875a822/sqlx-core/src/pool/inner.rs#L62) by the InnerPool prevent it from being dropped when a pool is created and dropped in quick succession. If an application uses code that creates and "quickly" discards a pool without manually closing the pool, connections in the pool will be leaked.

I think that the following are probably related to this:

- #1824
- #1862

And these _may_ be related:

- #2294
- #2249
- #1928

### Minimal Reproduction

```rust
use sqlx::{
    postgres::{PgConnectOptions, PgPoolOptions},
    query, Connection, PgConnection, query_scalar,
};

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() {
    let pg_options = PgConnectOptions::new()
        .host("127.0.0.1")
        .port(5432)
        .database("postgres")
        .username("postgres")
        .password("postgres");

    tokio::spawn({
        let options = pg_options.clone();
        async move {
            let pool = PgPoolOptions::new()
                .min_connections(10)
                .max_connections(10)
                .connect_with(options.application_name("leaky_connections"))
                .await
                .unwrap();

            query("SELECT 1").execute(&pool).await.unwrap();
        }
    })
    .await
    .unwrap();

    let mut conn = PgConnection::connect_with(&pg_options).await.unwrap();

    let count: i64 = query_scalar("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE application_name = $1")
        .bind("leaky_connections")
        .fetch_one(&mut conn)
        .await
        .unwrap();

    println!("{count} connections left open"); // prints 10 connections left open
}
```

```toml
[dependencies]
sqlx = { version = "0.6", features = ["runtime-tokio-rustls", "postgres"] }
tokio = { version = "1", features = ["full"] }
futures = "0.3"
```

### Info
* SQLx version: 0.62
* SQLx features enabled: "runtime-tokio-rustls", "postgres"
* Database server and version: postgres 14.7
* Operating system: macos
* `rustc --version`: 1.67.1
